' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. This one exercises the Phase 2
' construct set together: FOR-range, arithmetic (MOD), comparisons, nested
' IF, and PRINT of both string literals and computed integers -- not just
' single-construct probes.
'
' Classic FizzBuzz, 1 to 20. Nested IF rather than an ELSE IF chain (this
' dialect's ELSE IF support is unconfirmed for this shape; nested IF is the
' established safe pattern used throughout this codebase). Expected output
' verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this identical source
' as the equivalence-testing oracle.
FOR i = 1 TO 20
    IF i MOD 15 == 0 THEN
        PRINT "FizzBuzz"
    END IF
    IF i MOD 15 != 0 THEN
        IF i MOD 3 == 0 THEN
            PRINT "Fizz"
        END IF
        IF i MOD 3 != 0 THEN
            IF i MOD 5 == 0 THEN
                PRINT "Buzz"
            END IF
            IF i MOD 5 != 0 THEN
                PRINT i
            END IF
        END IF
    END IF
NEXT
